From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 10:19:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02800/11362] [outer-loop] FinAcumen routing refinement:
 confidence threshold + failure cautions (arXiv:2606.17642)

Folds the FinAcumen selective-experience-memory lessons into recommend_approach (additive, backward-
compatible). FinAcumen's key empirical finding: an IRRELEVANT retrieved example DEGRADES reasoning
(precision > recall), and a frozen 8B + thresholded experience memory rivals GPT-4o/72B. Applied to
our transfer-routing:
  - confident_transfer / routing_confidence: only few-shot the top solved-game recipe when the match
    clears the bar (>= an action-type match on the _similarity scale); below it, do NOT blind-copy a
    misleading recipe -> induce COLD via the strategy solver / graph-explore (the unseen LIVE game
    case correctly returns confident_transfer=False).
  - cautions: aggregate the top matches' failure dead-ends + general gotchas (FinAcumen's Cautions,
    the complement of the success Findings) so the runtime induction prompt is told what NOT to do,
    deduped + capped at 8.
Verified: tr87 (close match) -> confident_transfer=True conf=1.0; zz99_unseen -> False conf=0.0,
both with cautions. 5 tests pass incl. backward-compat (old keys retained). Directly de-risks the
"bad transfer is worse than no transfer" failure mode on held-out unseen games.

